{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064051 :question/id #uuid "90010ae5-e211-510f-b188-dc3006926d94" :question/math-academy-id "e-381" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int 5 \\cdot 9^x +3 e^x \\, \\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we combine the sum rule and our exponential rules to get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\displaystyle \\int 5 \\cdot 9^x +3 e^x  \\, \\textrm d x &= \\displaystyle 5\\int 9^x \\, \\textrm{d}x+ 3 \\displaystyle \\int e^x \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n&= 5\\cdot \\dfrac{9^x}{\\ln 9} + 3 e^x +C.\n}\n$$"}
